<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#cotton">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cotton</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cotton is a plant fibre spun and woven into textiles, one of the most important traded commodities in history. Indian cotton textiles were exported widely under the Gupta, Mughal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> empires, and cotton was cultivated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>. In the industrial era, cotton manufacturing was central to the economy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cotton.jpg" alt="Cotton" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: കാക്കര · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cotton_-_%E0%B4%AA%E0%B4%B0%E0%B5%81%E0%B4%A4%E0%B5%8D%E0%B4%A4%E0%B4%BF_03.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
